Certainly! Below is a simple HTML template for a basic webpage. This template includes the essential structure of an HTML document, including the `<!DOCTYPE html>` declaration, `<html>`, `<head>`, and `<body>` tags. It also includes some basic meta information and a simple title and content.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Basic Webpage</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
        }
        header, footer {
            background-color: #333;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 10px 0;
        }
        main {
            padding: 20px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Welcome to My Basic Webpage</h1>
    </header>
    <main>
        <h2>About This Page</h2>
        <p>This is a simple webpage created using HTML. It includes a header, main content area, and a footer.</p>
        <p>You can add more content here, such as images, lists, and links.</p>
    </main>
    <footer>
        <p>Copyright © 2023 My Basic Webpage</p>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
```

This template includes a simple CSS within the `<style>` tag to make the webpage look a bit more appealing. The CSS styles the body, header, footer, and main content area. You can modify the content and styles as needed to fit your specific requirements.
